\title{The Real Line Is Locally Compact}
\taxon{Example}
\p{
    For each #{x\in\mathbb{R}}, the closed interval
    #{K=[x-1,x+1]} is compact by
    [compactness of closed intervals](thm-001P). It contains the open interval
    #{(x-1,x+1)}, so #{K} is a neighborhood of #{x}. Therefore the Euclidean
    real line is [locally compact](def-005U).
}
